ckages/evals/tests/test_subject_call_floor.py", "packages/evals/tests/test_unanswered_calls.py", "packages/evals/tests/test_unreadable_run_refusals.py", "packages/evals/tests/test_usage_capture.py", "packages/evals/tests/test_wall_clock_ceilings.py", "packages/evals/tests/test_weakest_margin_and_reader_names.py", "packages/evals/tests/test_whole_run_reads_paged.py", "packages/evals/tests/test_witnessed_judging.py", "packages/evals/tests/test_writer_prompt_retired.py", "packages/evals/tests/toyhost_plan.py", "packages/registry/tests/unit/registry/test_unsigned_agent_concession_expires.py", "tests/enforcement/_model_literal_exemptions.txt", "tests/enforcement/_public_api_consumers.txt", "tests/enforcement/test_a_tool_states_its_notes_first.py"], "files_oracle": [], "findings": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "severity": "warning", "title": "The regression watch's judged tiers still read verbatim fields on their default path, though the CHANGELOG and docs say they no longer do", "recommendation": "RegressionWatch._judged_results (ops/regressions.py:332-335) has two branches. The commit elides only the narrowed one (one subject's runs). The other branch is the common case: no narrowing, or no subject. It still calls self.host.storage.query_eval_results(scope_id), which reads every result in the scope with world_events and kind_payload included. That read is held to READ_TIER_ROW_BUDGET by rows, not by bytes, which is the incident class this commit fixes. The new text in CHANGELOG.md says 'A regression watch's judged tiers read their runs the same way'. design.md says they 'read many runs' results in one read, without their verbatim fields'. adopting-a-host.md says the same. Each statement is true of one branch only, so an operator sizing a pod from the docs will under-provision for the scope-wide judged-tier read. The query_eval_results docstring (kernel/storage.py:2641) also says 'no projection ... every read is already narrow', which is stale now that results store verbatim fields. Scope: class. Fix by giving the scope-wide branch the same elision, for example a by-type read with exclude=VERBATIM_RESULT_FIELDS, and correct the docstring. Then search for other callers of query_eval_results(scope_id) that fold results into figures, because those are members of the same class outside this diff.", "files": ["packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/ops/regressions.py", "packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/kernel/storage.py", "CHANGELOG.md", "packages/evals/docs/design.md", "packages/evals/docs/adopting-a-host.md"], "fid": "R-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "warning", "title": "The bundle's measure walk does read world_events, so slim and whole bundles are equal only by accident, and the equality test cannot see the difference", "recommendation": "The commit claims that 'no reading of the bundle reads either' field. That is false at code level. analysis/bundle/measures.py _carrier_leaves (line 261) walks every list-of-BaseModel field of EvalResult, and RECORD_CARRIERS does not include world_events. With world_events present, the walk yields WorldEvent's scalar leaves into compute_measures (measures.py:808) and _mechanism_value (mechanisms.py:101): kind, dimension, condition, caused_by, event and the integer turn. Today these are no-ops only because no core measure has those names. A host whose MeasureRegistry describes a measure named 'turn', or a categorical 'event' or 'condition', gets three wrong results from a whole read. (1) It pools world-event values as observations of that measure under the carrier 'world_events[]'. (2) It flags undescribed numeric siblings as unreported. (3) It marks a same-named leaf from another carrier ambiguous and drops it. The elided read does none of these, so the bundle silently differs between the two read paths. test_the_bundle_is_the_one_a_whole_read_of_its_results_gives cannot detect this. Its WorldEvents leave turn=None and its profile registers no measures (MeasureRegistry(())), so every world_events leaf is an undescribed string or absent, and removing the elision would still pass. The other host callables that receive these results are not affected: shipped sweepable readers, judge tiers and judge_trial_of are only reachable outside the bundle, and the host contract in adopting-a-host.md already tells hosts that reader callables get results without these fields. Scope: instance. Make the two reads equal by construction: skip VERBATIM_RESULT_FIELDS in _carrier_leaves beside RECORD_CARRIERS. Then make the oracle able to fail: give the test's WorldEvents a turn and register a host measure named 'turn' in _PROFILE.", "files": ["packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/analysis/bundle/measures.py", "packages/evals/tests/test_bundle_read_leaves_out_verbatim_fields.py"], "fid": "R-2"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "warning", "title": "No test pins the regression watch's new elision", "recommendation": "Only the bundle's read is pinned (test_the_read_asks_the_store_to_leave_both_verbatim_fields_out). The narrowed judged-tier read is exercised by the existing TestTheRegressionWatchsJudgedTiersAreHeldToTheBudget tests, but none of them checks what that read asks the store to leave out. Deleting elide=VERBATIM_RESULT_FIELDS from ops/regressions.py:342-344 would pass every test, so the memory fix for that path has no regression guard. Scope: instance. Add a recording store, like _RecordsExclude, to one narrowed judged-step test in test_aggregate_read_budget.py and assert that the read of eval_result excludes both fields. If the scope-wide branch from the first finding is fixed, assert it there as well. That file's class docstring at line 659 ('read the subject's results whole') becomes stale with this change. It is inert prose and needs no separate edit.", "files": ["packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/ops/regressions.py", "packages/evals/tests/test_aggregate_read_budget.py"], "fid": "R-3"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "warning", "title": "No test evidence recorded for this tree", "recommendation": "`prawduct-hook test-status` exits 1 with 'stale: no .test-evidence.json on disk'. This is a cumulative review, so the suite is owed for HEAD d047f046c before the change lands. Run the gate on the testament pool and record evidence. Scope: none.", "fid": "R-4"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Unintended", "severity": "note", "title": "CampaignReadStore implementers outside this repo must add `elide`, and the CHANGELOG files this under Added", "recommendation": "Inside the repo the port and its implementers agree. EvalStorage, ToyhostStorage and _StampedStore all accept a keyword `elide` defaulting to (). _StampedStore forwards it, and ToyhostStorage's model_copy(update=dict.fromkeys(elide)) matches the store's 'each reads as none' behaviour. assemble_context_bundle always passes elide=, though. A host that implements the provisional CampaignReadStore with its own class rather than EvalStorage will get a TypeError on its next bundle. The CHANGELOG puts this under 'Added' and does not tell implementers what they must change. Scope: instance. State in the CHANGELOG entry that implementers of the port must accept `elide`.", "files": ["CHANGELOG.md", "packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/analysis/bundle/assemble.py"], "fid": "R-5"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "severity": "note", "title": "record-lint suite-total-claim: r2-config-sweep.md line 3 is a false positive", "recommendation": "This NOTE is relayed from record_lint. The flagged '200 test' text is part of '1,200 test cases', the size of a synthetic eval's case set. It is not a test-suite total. Nothing reads it and no edit is wanted. Scope: none.", "files": ["packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/analysis/analyst/skill/exemplars/r2-config-sweep.md"], "fid": "R-6"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "severity": "warning", "title": "An elided EvalResult is unmarked and writable, unlike the elided EvalRun precedent beside it", "recommendation": "Class. The store port now hands back EvalResult copies whose world_events/kind_payload read as None. Nothing on the object says they were left out, and save_eval_result/replace_eval_result accept such a copy, which would delete the stored verbatim fields. The run-side precedent in the same storage class does both things this lacks. load_eval_runs(elide_payload=...) records the elision with EvalRun.note_elided_payload/elided_payload_paths, and save_eval_run refuses an elided run (storage.py ~2003-2008, 'Writing it back would delete them'). The ambiguity is not hypothetical: judge_kind_readings treats kind_payload None as 'it carries no judge trial' (analysis/judge_kind_readings.py:317-322). A future bundle lens or tier that reads a verbatim field over this read would misclassify every result silently and never error. Today no consumer of the bundle or of the judged tiers reads either field, and the judge writers reload whole before replace. So this is a hazard in the design, not a live bug. Construction: record the elision on the result, the way EvalRun does (a private elided-fields attribute set in query_eval_results_by_runs), and make save/replace refuse a result that carries it. Same remedy, cheaper: narrow the parameter from an open `elide: Sequence[str]` to the one set callers pass (e.g. `verbatim: bool = True`, or `elide: frozenset[Literal['world_events','kind_payload']]`). As written, any field name is accepted, and eliding a required field (eval_run_id, test_case_id) fails hydration instead of 'reading as none' as the docstring promises. The name/shape also diverges from the sibling `elide_payload: frozenset[str]`.", "files": ["packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/kernel/storage.py", "packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/analysis/bundle/assemble.py", "packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/kernel/run_pages.py"], "fid": "R-7"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "severity": "warning", "title": "Regression watch's _judged_results elides on one branch only; docs say the judged tiers read without verbatim fields", "recommendation": "Instance. RegressionWatch._judged_results has two branches (ops/regressions.py ~329-346). The narrowed branch now reads with elide=VERBATIM_RESULT_FIELDS. The un-narrowed branch still calls self.host.storage.query_eval_results(scope_id), which ships every result of the whole scope whole, verbatim fields included. That branch's read is held to READ_TIER_ROW_BUDGET by rows, not bytes, and bytes per row are the mechanism this commit fixes. So the one function returns two result shapes, and the larger exposure is the one left whole. The changed prose claims the whole: CHANGELOG ('A regression watch's judged tiers read their runs the same way'), docs/design.md ('a regression watch's judged tiers still read many runs' results in one read, without their verbatim fields') and docs/adopting-a-host.md. Fix: route the un-narrowed branch through a projected read too, either an elide on query_eval_results or the by-type read with exclude. query_eval_results' own docstring ('every read is already narrow', storage.py ~2641) is contradicted by this commit's premise; delete that claim when touching it. Otherwise, make the prose say only the narrowed read elides.", "files": ["packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/ops/regressions.py", "packages/evals/docs/design.md", "packages/evals/docs/adopting-a-host.md", "CHANGELOG.md"], "fid": "R-8"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "severity": "note", "title": "VERBATIM_RESULT_FIELDS made public by name but left out of run_pages.__all__", "recommendation": "Instance. Dropping the underscore is justified by production use: assemble.py and regressions.py now import it, which meets the stability-contract rule's 'promote only when production code needs it'. The CHANGELOG says it is 'public now'. But run_pages.__all__ lists every other public name of the module and not this one. Add it to __all__ so the module's declared surface matches its names.", "files": ["packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/kernel/run_pages.py"], "fid": "R-9"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "severity": "note", "title": "Release note: this adds API after v0.83.0, so the release carrying it is a minor; this PR correctly does not bump", "recommendation": "Scope none. v0.83.0 is tagged and the workspace is at 0.83.0. This commit adds a keyword to EvalStorage.query_eval_results_by_runs and to the CampaignReadStore protocol, and newly exposes VERBATIM_RESULT_FIELDS. Per CLAUDE.md, an intra-family API addition ships in a MINOR bump (tests/enforcement/test_api_growth_requires_a_minor_bump.py), so this must ship as 0.84.0, not 0.83.1. Per the repo rule that work PRs never bump, no version change belongs in this PR, and none is made. One more fact for the maintainer: CampaignReadStore is provisional (surface.json records no signature, and no host import list names it), so the protocol change needs no MIGRATIONS record. A host's own CampaignReadStore without `elide` would now TypeError, though. Every in-repo implementer was updated: EvalStorage, ToyhostStorage, _StampedStore. Every test DocumentStore subclass that overrides by_doc_type forwards exclude, so parity holds.", "files": ["packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/analysis/bundle/assemble.py", "CHANGELOG.md"], "fid": "R-10"}, {"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "severity": "warning", "title": "An elided result is indistinguishable from one that had no world or payload, and nothing but prose and a narrow equality fixture stops a later bundle or tier reader from reading one", "recommendation": "Scope: class. The elision is documented everywhere it should be: the read-site comment in assemble.py, the CampaignReadStore.query_eval_results_by_runs and EvalStorage docstrings, design.md, adopting-a-host.md (including that host callables such as a sweepable's `read` and `row_columns` get results without the two fields), and the CHANGELOG. Nothing structural enforces it, though. An elided result carries `world_events=None` and `kind_payload=None`, and None already has a meaning there: the runner writes `world_events=None` when 'no world was opened', and run/regrade.py reads `result.world_events is not None` as has_events. Runs handle the same problem structurally: EvalRun.elided_payload_paths records what a read left out, and production_footing raises on an elided run. Results have no such marker. Here is the case that would slip through. A maintainer adds a bundle or judged-tier lens that reads Firings.of(result.world_events), or calls judge_kind_readings, which reads result.kind_payload, over the bundle's results. Or a host declares a result-level sweepable reader that reads kind_payload. That code silently computes 'no world, no trial' rather than failing. The equality test would not catch it: its _PROFILE has an empty MeasureRegistry and SHARED_CORE sweepables, and its campaign declares no goal or world checks, so nothing in the fixture could read the verbatim fields even when they ship. Its oracle is therefore 'equal for this profile', not 'no reader looks'. The same class covers run_pages.without_payloads and results_without_payloads. Closing it takes a construction, not more prose. Option one: have the store-side elision and without_payloads record which fields they left out on the result (the analogue of elided_payload_paths), and make the readers of world_events and kind_payload (judge_trial_of, Firings.of, regrade) refuse a result that has them elided. Option two, if that is too wide: make the equality fixture exercise readers that do look, such as a sweepable reader and a world check that read the verbatim fields, so the test fails the moment any bundle path depends on them.", "files": ["packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/analysis/bundle/assemble.py", "packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/kernel/run_pages.py", "packages/evals/tests/test_bundle_read_leaves_out_verbatim_fields.py", "packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/ops/regressions.py"], "fid": "R-11"}, {"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "severity": "warning", "title": "CHANGELOG and design.md say the regression watch's judged tiers read without the verbatim fields; the scope-wide branch still reads every result whole", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. RegressionWatch._judged_results has two branches. Only the subject-narrowed branch passes elide=VERBATIM_RESULT_FIELDS. When the history read the whole scope (`narrowed is None or subject_id is None`), it still calls self.host.storage.query_eval_results(scope_id), which issues a by_doc_type with no exclude and ships world_events and kind_payload for every result in the scope. The shipped CHANGELOG says 'A regression watch's judged tiers read their runs the same way', and design.md says 'a regression watch's judged tiers still read many runs' results in one read, without their verbatim fields'. That is false for the scope-wide case, which is the larger of the two reads. An operator sizing a pod, or a maintainer chasing the next memory incident, will trust the claim and look elsewhere. Fix it one of two ways. Elide on the scope branch too, by giving query_eval_results an elide or exclude that reaches by_doc_type. Or narrow the CHANGELOG and design.md sentences to the subject-narrowed read.", "files": ["packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/ops/regressions.py", "CHANGELOG.md", "packages/evals/docs/design.md"], "fid": "R-12"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "warning", "title": "CampaignReadStore gained a required keyword that a host's own structural implementation must accept, recorded only as 'Added'", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. CampaignReadStore is structural, and its docstring invites a host's own storage to satisfy it by having the methods. assemble_context_bundle now always calls query_eval_results_by_runs(..., elide=VERBATIM_RESULT_FIELDS). Any host whose own implementation predates `elide` (the shape the toyhost fixture and test_output_bound_labels' _StampedStore had until this commit) now fails at bundle assembly with a 